    {
      "id": "1561594420758061170",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T04:18:42.93+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "If you'd want to help, a non-expensive 1% (ish) LDO that can do like 50 mA at outputs programmable from two digital RPiPico2 pins and voltages from at least like 3~3.4 ish Volts down to at LEAST 500 mV, ideally I'd want it down to about 300 mV. \nIdeally one that's stocked at JLCPCB, but worst case their ability to order from mouser/digikey at a unit price premium and handle the logistics for you would give that as an escape but I'd prefer not to, due to it being prone to delays.\n\n[Mostly I'm not sure if the SRAM control can behave itself enough at the very low voltage end; I'd probably expect most cells to retain even at very very low supply.]",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
