    {
      "id": "1561604310607986689",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T04:58:00.854+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "@Lauri  you wrote this in `src/hal/mux.cpp`; does this mean it's currently suffering the slow behavior but could do the fast if one edits in a mythical (doesn't seem particularly specified here, but I'd guess it's imported/included from platformio?) header file?\n\nBecause looking at the timing diagram in the datasheet we could let the falling clock coincide with the data transition.\n\nI know you don't need it to be very fast, due to your fairly high-Z measurements, but for the FlexMem testing I'd like to be at least somewhat near the MUX chip's potential speed.\n\n```\n// Speed note: replace digitalWrite with gpio_set_mask/gpio_clr_mask (hardware/gpio.h)\n// for ~50x speedup (~200 ns/transaction vs ~10 µs). All CH446X setup/hold\n// requirements (3–10 ns) are met by back-to-back SIO writes without added delays.\n```",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-10_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
      },
