    {
      "id": "1561633427436998668",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T06:53:42.847+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Ohh ok good thx.\nDo you happen to know if the bond tester that's said to be tentatively scheduled to be sent to me (once I commit to teaching it FlexMem bitcell stress-testing) is in China?\n\nWould you consider the expansion header to be reasonable to put a programmable LDO on to support as here some testing at less than the 3.3V?\n\nOfc it's inherently a limited architecture with the MUX but it could be so much worse \uD83D\uDE04 .\nAnd letting such simple checking be done by it should enable us to do much better testing for a bunch of chips even if it's somewhat awkward to pull off.",
      "author": {
