    {
      "id": "1561682145075011708",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T10:07:18.037+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I've figured out a way to do programmable LDO with commodity parts: a 12 bit I2C DAC and an \"adjustable\"-style LDO, and a 3-resistor weighted summer mixing Vout/GND/Vdac at the LDO's FB node.\nShould easily give about 1mV steps from around 50 mV to around 3.2-ish V.\n\nWell, technically Gemini did the looking for me but I'm pretty sure those parts are actually commodity (or very similar ones at least).\n\nI wasn't planning on deleting the pull-up but rather adding a preload to GND to overpower R12 and give the LDO some nicer operating conditions.\n\nI'll try to get a layout on Wednesday; if there's no plan yet regarding what kind of header that is, may I request that to be decreed by then to allow including a matching connector and board orientation to go with it?\n\nAny preference about I2C assignment to the two GPIOs on the header? I'd put one of them simple EEPROMs on it I guess...\n\nShould I provide precise 3.3V on it as well or would that be counter-productive due to how invasive the changes to the tester board would be for custom 3v3 supply? I could probably go for just calibrating the ADC by muxing COMA and COME together, I'd hope the existing 3v3 reference doesn't drift wildly within a minute or so at least...",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-10_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
