    {
      "id": "1562349178619695267",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:17:51.227+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "@Tim 'mithro' Ansell Stuart Said to ask you for approval first.\n\nI'd like to draw up a simple add-on board tomorrow with an I2C DAC, an I2C serial/eeprom/-style chip (for calibration and/or such), an adjustable LDO, 3 resistors summing these together to create a programmable LDO from it, and probably a somewhat decent (at least in drift over time and temperature) voltage reference for the LDO and the I2C DAC.\n\nI'd prefer to get JLC to assemble a pack of 5 and ship them to where the bond testers are; I'd request two of them for me to be bundled with the tester and (assuming they'd conveniently meet the COBs) 2 of each FlexMem COB; I'd be willing to donate the rest of the assembled \"programmable LDO\" tester-add-on modules.\n\nOnce I have a system quote from JLC (needs the board to pass their automated DRC) we could discuss if you'd want to order from them or if I'd order it shipped to you or what (whichever you'd like, I don't need a decision before I'm ready to place the order anyways). I'd expect it to be like 25$ or such for the 5-pack anyways.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-10_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
      },
      "attachments": [],
